==Analysis ==
[[File:2020 Moldovan presidential election map.svg|450px|thumb|right|Results of the 2020 Moldovan presidential election. The left map shows the winner in the first round by territorial electoral commissions. The right map shows the winner in the second round by territorial electoral commissions.]]

The first round of the election was characterized by a historically high turnout of the [[Moldovan diaspora|diaspora]]. Moldovans living abroad were responsible for 15% of the cast ballots.<ref>{{Cite web|title=/VIDEO/ Record, stabilit de diasporă. Pentru prima dată în istoria țării, 15% din alegătorii care și-au exprimat votul au fost din străinătate|url=https://tv8.md/2020/11/02/video-record-stabilit-de-diaspora-pentru-prima-data-in-istoria-tarii-15-din-alegatorii-care-si-au-exprimat-votul-au-fost-din-strainatate/|access-date=2020-11-16|language=ro-RO}}</ref> As [[expatriate]]s voted overwhelmingly for Maia Sandu, their high turnout is considered one of the main reasons for her first-round win. Because most polls gave an edge to incumbent president Dodon, Maia Sandu's result was considered unexpected by experts.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Moldova: Pro-EU candidate scores surprise first-round win|url=https://euobserver.com/foreign/149953|access-date=2020-11-16|website=EUobserver|language=en}}</ref> Multiple analysts voiced the opinion that Renato Usatîi, who came in third and positioned himself as a [[Centrism|centrist]], was expected to play a decisive role in the second round by announcing his support for one of the two candidates.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Opinie: O parte din alegătorii lui Usatîi vor vota nu pentru Maia Sandu, ci împotriva lui Dodon|url=https://deschide.md/ro/stiri/alegeri/74787/Opinie-O-parte-din-alegătorii-lui-Usatîi-vor-vota-nu-pentru-Maia-Sandu-ci-împotriva-lui-Dodon.htm|access-date=2020-11-16|website=Deschide.MD|language=ro}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Concluzii după primul tur și scenarii pentru turul doi|work=Today|url=http://today.md/2020/11/02/concluzii-dupa-primul-tur-si-scenarii-pentru-turul-doi/|access-date=2020-11-16|language=en-US|archive-date=2020-11-19|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201119100801/http://today.md/2020/11/02/concluzii-dupa-primul-tur-si-scenarii-pentru-turul-doi/|url-status=dead}}</ref> Usatîi later advised people who voted for him to vote against Dodon in the second round.

An exit poll from the day of the second round suggested Sandu had won with 54.8% of the vote.<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20201115195703/https://uk.reuters.com/article/uk-moldova-election-exitpolls-idUKKBN27V0NW Pro-EU candidate Sandu leads in Moldova presidential election run-off - exit poll] Reuters, 15 November 2020</ref> The actual results (released later) showed Sandu winning by a larger margin, with 57.72% of the vote.<ref name=":0" /><ref name=":1" /> Sandu's victory was again helped by her lead in the diaspora's vote. Sandu nevertheless won 51% of votes on Moldova alone.<ref>{{cite web|title=Separate ways: Contrasting elections in Georgia and Moldova|url=https://ecfr.eu/article/seperate-ways-contrasting-elections-in-georgia-and-moldova/|website=ECFR|language=en|access-date=18 December 2020|publication-date=}}.</ref>

==Aftermath==
===International reactions===
*{{flag|Azerbaijan}}: President  [[Ilham Aliyev]] congratulated Sandu through a letter and expressed his faith that the relations between Azerbaijan and Moldova will continue to develop and expand.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://menafn.com/1101144022/President-of-Azerbaijan-sends-letter-to-President-elect-of-Moldova|title=President of Azerbaijan sends letter to President-elect of Moldova|newspaper=MENAFN|date=18 November 2020}}</ref>
*{{flag|Belarus}}: President [[Alexander Lukashenko]] congratulated Sandu, saying that the hoped to "enrich bilateral relations" between Moldova and Belarus with "new creative initiatives".<ref>{{cite web |url=https://eng.belta.by/president/view/lukashenko-sends-greetings-to-moldova-president-elect-maia-sandu-135077-2020/ |title=Lukashenko sends greetings to Moldova president-elect Maia Sandu |website=eng.belta.by |accessdate=21 November 2020}}</ref> Opposition leader [[Sviatlana Tsikhanouskaya]] also congratulated Sandu, saying that she was "deeply impressed with her bravery and dedication".<ref>{{cite web |url=https://tv8.md/2020/11/16/svetlana-tihanovskaia-mesaj-de-felicitare-pentru-maia-sandu-sunt-impresionata-de-daruirea-ei/ |title=Svetlana Tihanovskaia, mesaj de felicitare pentru Maia Sandu: "Sunt impresionată de dăruirea ei" |website=tv8.md |accessdate=21 November 2020 |language=ro}}</ref>
*{{flag|France}}: President [[Emmanuel Macron]] congratulated Sandu emphasizing France's ongoing support for Moldova's European integration efforts.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.jurnal.md/ro/news/13a325b89112e815/emmanuel-macron-scrisoare-catre-presedintele-ales-maia-sandu.html |title=Emmanuel Macron, scrisoare către președintele ales Maia Sandu |website=jurnal.md |language=ro |accessdate=21 November 2020}}</ref>
*{{flag|Germany}}: Chancellor [[Angela Merkel]] congratulated Sandu on her "strong mandate" and wished her success in dealing with the multiple issues Moldova was facing.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.jurnal.md/ro/news/a58df0e61d0cc939/angela-merkel-mesaj-de-felicitare-pentru-maia-sandu-ma-bucur-ca-cetatenii-din-moldova-v-au-dat-un-mandat-puternic.html |title=Angela Merkel, mesaj de felicitare pentru Maia Sandu: "Mă bucur că cetățenii din Moldova v-au dat un mandat puternic" |website=jurnal.md |accessdate=21 November 2020 |language=ro}}</ref>
*{{flag|Italy}}: President [[Sergio Mattarella]] congratulated Sandu, saying that he hoped to "further consolidate the excellent relationship" between Italy and Moldova.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.zdg.md/stiri/presedintele-italiei-a-felicitat-o-pe-maia-sandu-cu-ocazia-victoriei-in-alegerile-prezidentiale/ |title=Președintele Italiei a felicitat-o pe Maia Sandu cu ocazia victoriei în alegerile prezidențiale |website=zdg.md |accessdate=21 November 2020 |language=ro}}</ref>
*{{flag|Latvia}}: President [[Egils Levits]] contacted Sandu to congratulate her on the election win. In the discussion, Levits emphasized Latvia's continued assistance to Moldova in the reform process.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.ipn.md/en/president-latvia-congratulates-newly-elected-president-of-moldova-7965_1077795.html |title=President Latvia congratulates newly elected President of Moldova |website=ipn.md |accessdate=21 November 2020}}</ref>
*{{flag|Oman}}: Sultan [[Haitham bin Tariq Al Said]] expressed his congratulations to Sandu for winning the elections and his desire to improve relations between Moldova and Oman.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://omannews.gov.om/NewsDescription/ArtMID/392/ArticleID/23553|title=HM The Sultan Congratulates New President of Moldova|newspaper=[[Oman News Agency]]|date=19 November 2020}}</ref>
*{{flag|Poland}}: President [[Andrzej Duda]] congratulated Sandu and said that Poland was "determined to strengthen high-level Moldovan-Polish relations both on bilateral and European level".<ref>{{cite web |url=https://tv8.md/2020/11/16/presedintele-poloniei-a-felicitat-o-pe-maia-sandu-polonia-este-hotarata-sa-consolideze-relatiile-la-nivel-inalt/ |title=Președintele Poloniei a felicitat-o pe Maia Sandu: "Polonia este hotărâtă să consolideze relațiile la nivel înalt" |website=tv8.md |accessdate=21 November 2020 |language=ro}}</ref>
*{{flag|Romania}}: President [[Klaus Iohannis]] was the first [[head of state]] to congratulate Sandu on her victory, doing this through a phone call and [[Twitter]]. It was announced that Iohannis would visit Chișinău once Sandu assumed the presidential office and Moldova's integration path into the EU was discussed.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.digi24.ro/stiri/externe/moldova/klaus-iohannis-primul-sef-de-stat-care-o-felicita-pe-maia-sandu-pentru-castigarea-alegerilor-1402481|title=Klaus Iohannis a discutat la telefon cu Maia Sandu. Șeful statului va avea o vizită oficială la Chișinău|newspaper=[[Digi24]]|date=16 November 2020|language=ro}}</ref> Later, Prime Minister [[Ludovic Orban]] also congratulated Sandu.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.hotnews.ro/stiri-esential-24421614-ludovic-orban-crezut-inceput-maia-sandu-asistam-eveniment-adevarat-istoric-pentru-republica-moldova.htm|title=Ludovic Orban: Am crezut de la început în Maia Sandu. Asistăm la un eveniment cu-adevărat istoric pentru Republica Moldova|newspaper=Hotnews.ro|date=16 November 2020|language=ro}}</ref>
*{{flag|Russia}}: President [[Vladimir Putin]] sent a telegram congratulating Sandu and looking forward to "constructive development of relations".<ref>{{Cite web|title=Putin congratulates Maia Sandu on winning Moldovan presidential election|url=https://tass.com/politics/1224111|access-date=2020-11-17|website=TASS}}</ref> Opposition leader [[Alexei Navalny]] also congratulated Sandu, saying that he welcomed the election of a president who would fight corruption.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://protv.md/politic/aleksei-navalnii-felicitari-maia-sandu-moldova-are-totul-pentru-o-dezvoltare-de-succes---2547220.html |title=Aleksei Navalnii:"Felicitari Maia Sandu! Moldova are totul pentru o dezvoltare de succes" |accessdate=21 November 2020 |website=protv.md |language=ro}}</ref> [[Patriarch Kirill of Moscow]] congratulated Sandu as well, saying that he wished for "the continuation of a productive interaction between the authorities and the [[Eastern Orthodox Church]] in Moldova".<ref>{{cite web |url=https://unimedia.info/ro/news/da53d60b0f5aa8bf/patriarhul-rusiei-kirill-a-felicitat-o-pe-maia-sandu-cu-ocazia-victoriei-in-alegerile-prezidentiale-ce-urari-i-a-transmis.html |title=Patriarhul Rusiei Kirill a felicitat-o pe Maia Sandu cu ocazia victoriei în alegerile prezidențiale. Ce urări i-a transmis |website=unimedia.info |accessdate=21 November 2020 |language=ro}}</ref>
*{{flag|Ukraine}}: President [[Volodymyr Zelenskyy]] was the second head of state to congratulate Sandu. He said that he was looking forward to strengthening the relations between Moldova and Ukraine on their path to the [[European Union]] membership during Sandu's presidency.<ref>{{cite news |title=Зеленський привітав Санду з перемогою на президентських виборах |url=https://www.eurointegration.com.ua/news/2020/11/16/7116552/ |accessdate=16 November 2020 |work=Європейська правда |date=16 November 2020 |language=uk}}</ref>

===Fraud allegations===
Moldovan President Igor Dodon alleged multiple voting irregularities including the prevention of Transnistrians from voting, organized transportation of voters in EU countries and interference from foreign leaders.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://stiri.md/article/politica/dodon-va-contesta-rezultatele-alegerilor-felicit-preliminar-oponenta |title=Dodon va contesta rezultatele alegerilor: Felicit preliminar oponenta |website=stiri.md |accessdate=21 November 2020 |language=ro}}</ref> Dodon said that he would consider conceding defeat if the courts found nothing inappropriate in the voting process. He said "if the courts found that everything is okay, then we will put a full stop there". He also said that he was congratulating Sandu as a precaution.<ref>{{Cite web|date=15 November 2020|title=Moldova election: Pro-EU Maia Sandu wins presidency|url=https://www.dw.com/en/moldova-election-pro-eu-maia-sandu-wins-presidency/a-55611249|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201116002517/https://www.dw.com/en/moldova-election-pro-eu-maia-sandu-wins-presidency/a-55611249 |archive-date=2020-11-16 |access-date=2020-11-17|website=[[Deutsche Welle]]|language=en-GB}}</ref>

In 2021, leaked documents from the German newspaper ''[[Bild]]'' showed Russia supported the campaign for the 2020 Moldovan presidential election of Dodon and other candidates considered "friendly" to the country. According to these claims, Russia would have spent some 11.4 million euros, 4 million of which would have directly gone for Dodon and the other candidates themselves. Similar claims were made by Usatîi already in November 2020. PSRM denied these claims and announced it would file a lawsuit against the German newspaper and all Moldovan media "that took part in the dissemination of this blatant slander".<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.intellinews.com/leaked-documents-indicate-russia-spent-11-4mn-ahead-of-moldovan-presidential-election-214128/|title=Leaked documents indicate Russia spent €11.4mn ahead of Moldovan presidential election|first=Iulian|last=Ernst|newspaper=[[bne IntelliNews]]|date=25 June 2021}}</ref>

